1
00:00:00,751 --> 00:00:02,294
Oh, hey, Joey.

2
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,963
Mmm. Hey.

3
00:00:04,003 --> 00:00:06,131
Listen, um, I need
to ask you something.

4
00:00:06,173 --> 00:00:08,216
Okay, you know
how my stepdad's in prison?

5
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,427
Yeah.
Yeah, well,

6
00:00:10,469 --> 00:00:13,514
um, listen, he was supposed
to get a weekend furlough

7
00:00:13,555 --> 00:00:15,349
so he could come
to the wedding tomorrow,

8
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:19,311
but he just called and, well,
apparently, stabbing "Iceman"

9
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:20,771
in the exercise yard

10
00:00:20,813 --> 00:00:22,230
just couldn't wait
until Monday, so...

11
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:24,023
So, he can't come?

12
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,776
No.

13
00:00:25,818 --> 00:00:28,111
And so there's no one
to walk me down the aisle,

14
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:31,740
and, well, I would just really
love it if you would do it.

15
00:00:31,782 --> 00:00:34,409
Seriously?

16
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:37,287
Yeah. You've, you know,
sort of been like a dad to me.

17
00:00:39,623 --> 00:00:41,375
I mean, you've always,
you know, looked out for me

18
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,501
and shared your wisdom.

19
00:00:45,004 --> 00:00:48,256
I am pretty wisdomous.

20
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:51,010
So, what do you say?

21
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:55,472
Are you kidding?
Phoebe, I would be honored.

22
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:57,599
Oh... thank you.

23
00:00:57,641 --> 00:00:59,309
Ooh...

24
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:00,811
I hope...

25
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:04,606
I hope you know how much
you mean to me.

26
00:01:04,648 --> 00:01:07,651
Listen. I hope...

27
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:09,528
I hope that you know...

28
00:01:11,989 --> 00:01:13,699
I don't want you
to see your father cry.

29
00:01:13,741 --> 00:01:15,534
Go to your room!

30
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:27,170
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

31
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,381
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

32
00:01:29,423 --> 00:01:33,010
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

33
00:01:33,052 --> 00:01:37,056
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

34
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:39,224
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

35
00:01:39,266 --> 00:01:41,560
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

36
00:01:41,602 --> 00:01:45,397
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

37
00:01:45,439 --> 00:01:47,942
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

38
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:50,485
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

39
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:53,196
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

40
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:55,908
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

41
00:01:55,950 --> 00:02:01,663
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

42
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,335
Oh, here.

43
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,128
Oh, no, no, no.
Let your dad get this.

44
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,213
Ah...

45
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:11,548
( phone rings )

46
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,551
Oh...

47
00:02:14,593 --> 00:02:17,429
It's my wedding planner.
She's driving me crazy.

48
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,098
Hello.

49
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:22,225
Hey, okay, stop screaming.

50
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:26,105
Okay, so halibut.

51
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:27,982
All right, so salmon,
either way, I don't...

52
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:29,316
It doesn't matter to me!

53
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:31,192
Well, it matters to me!

54
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,655
Well...

55
00:02:34,696 --> 00:02:36,239
I don't care,
so you pick.

56
00:02:36,281 --> 00:02:39,868
Did you just hang up on me?

57
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,662
All right, look, I need you
at the rehearsal dinner

58
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:43,162
tonight at 1800 hours.

59
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:45,540
Uh-huh. Okay.
What time is that?

60
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:48,710
You don't know military time?

61
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:50,587
I must have been
in missile training

62
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:52,047
the day they taught that.

63
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:54,758
Just subtract 12.

64
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:58,137
Okay, so, 1,800
minus 12 is...

65
00:02:58,177 --> 00:03:00,097
1,788...

66
00:03:00,139 --> 00:03:01,431
Six o'clock!
Okay.

67
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:02,557
( phone rings )

68
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,267
Hold on. Yeah.
Geller here.

69
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:09,898
No, I said it has to be there
by 4:00. Good-bye.

70
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,733
God, how hard is it to make
an ice sculpture?

71
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:13,861
Ice sculpture?
That sounds really fancy.

72
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:16,071
I told you, I just
want a simple wedding.

73
00:03:16,113 --> 00:03:19,282
Please. Honey, leave
the details to me.

74
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:21,785
Now, I want to make this day
as special for you as I can.

75
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,078
Now, okay, I
was thinking

76
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,079
that the harpist
should wear white.

77
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,622
Well, harpist?

78
00:03:25,664 --> 00:03:27,666
My friend Marjorie
is playing the steel drums.

79
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:29,543
Oh, she backed out.

80
00:03:29,584 --> 00:03:30,627
She did? Why?

81
00:03:30,669 --> 00:03:31,712
I made her.

82
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,298
Steel drums don't really
say elegant wedding,

83
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,467
nor does Marjorie's
overwhelming scent.

84
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:41,972
Hey. She will shower
when Tibet is free.

85
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:52,566
Hey. You look great.

86
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,233
Hey. You, too.

87
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:55,944
I'm so glad we're
having this rehearsal dinner.

88
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,863
You know, I so rarely
get to practice my meals

89
00:03:57,905 --> 00:03:59,531
before I eat them.

90
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:02,659
Okay, what did we say
was your one gift to us?

91
00:04:02,701 --> 00:04:04,203
No stupid jokes.

92
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:06,413
But I thought that
was for the actual wedding.

93
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:08,456
Rehearse it.

94
00:04:08,498 --> 00:04:10,125
Hi.

95
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:11,752
Thanks for coming,
you guys.

96
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:12,878
Oh, yeah. Oh.

97
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:15,089
I, uh, I was,
uh, I was going

98
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:16,757
for a handshake.

99
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,592
Is that why your hand
is pressed against my crotch?

100
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:19,927
That is why.
Yeah.

101
00:04:22,387 --> 00:04:23,346
Rach?
Yeah?

102
00:04:23,388 --> 00:04:24,347
Where's Emma?

103
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:25,348
Oh, Monica made me send her

104
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,892
to my mother's.

105
00:04:26,934 --> 00:04:29,477
Apparently, babies
and weddings don't mix.

106
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:32,689
Are you still crying
about your damn baby?

107
00:04:32,731 --> 00:04:33,941
Phoebes...

108
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,109
you got to keep
the line moving.

109
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:37,111
Remember, 20
seconds per person.

110
00:04:37,152 --> 00:04:39,029
You see these clowns
all the time.

111
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,034
Hey, you're
Mike's parents, right?

112
00:04:44,076 --> 00:04:45,786
Yes, we are.

113
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:48,747
Gosh, our little ones are
growing up fast, huh?

114
00:04:50,082 --> 00:04:51,708
How's that?

115
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,127
You know, on the one hand,
you're happy for them,

116
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:55,462
but on the other hand,
it's hard to let go.

117
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,381
Who in God's name are you?

118
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,676
Hey, I'm not that fond
of you either, okay, buddy,

119
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,804
but I'm just trying
to be nice for the kids.

120
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:07,474
You know what
I just realized?

121
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,017
We have no idea
what we're doing

122
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,644
in the wedding tomorrow.

123
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:12,062
Yeah, I thought
we'd be groomsmen,

124
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:13,730
but wouldn't they
have asked us by now?

125
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:16,650
When did they ask you
to be a bridesmaid?

126
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:17,943
Uh, November.

127
00:05:17,985 --> 00:05:20,487
I want to say
it's not looking good.

128
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:21,780
Hey, Phoebes?

129
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,364
Sorry?

130
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:24,616
You haven't told these guys
what they're doing

131
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:25,617
in the wedding yet.

132
00:05:27,619 --> 00:05:29,412
Um, well, they're
not in the wedding.

133
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:31,581
What?

134
00:05:35,127 --> 00:05:37,420
Well...

135
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,631
this is really awkward.

136
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:41,716
Oh, and I can leave.

137
00:05:42,801 --> 00:05:45,095
I'm sorry, you guys,

138
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:47,264
but, you know,
Mike's got his brother

139
00:05:47,306 --> 00:05:50,600
and his friends from school,
so, you know, you were...

140
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:52,936
If it helps,
you were next in line.

141
00:05:52,978 --> 00:05:54,604
You just missed the cut.

142
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,148
Oh, man.

143
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:59,609
This is like figure skating team
all over again.

144
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:04,823
I mean, synchronized swimming.

145
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:08,118
I mean...
I mean, the balance beam.

146
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,203
Help me.
Football.

147
00:06:09,244 --> 00:06:11,038
Thank you.

148
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:14,249
Oh, Phoebes. Spit that out.
That has pork in it.

149
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:16,043
Oh!

150
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:18,461
I thought the pot stickers
were supposed to be vegetarian.

151
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:22,257
Yeah. I changed them.
I sent you a fax about it.

152
00:06:22,299 --> 00:06:24,176
I don't have a fax machine.

153
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:27,971
Huh. Well, then there are going
to be a few surprises.

154
00:06:30,057 --> 00:06:31,516
I can't believe
we're going to be

155
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:33,935
the only people that
aren't in this wedding.

156
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:36,104
I know. I hate being
left out of things.

157
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:37,564
And it's a wedding.

158
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:40,067
It'll be weird
if I'm not in it.

159
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:44,112
Hey, guys. How's it going?
Fine.

160
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:46,614
We're just sitting here,
alone, doing nothing.

161
00:06:46,656 --> 00:06:49,868
It's our rehearsal for tomorrow.

162
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,495
Yeah, look, about tomorrow,
I've got a question for you.

163
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:53,955
I just found out
that one of my groomsman

164
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:55,623
had an emergency
and can't make it.

165
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:56,624
What happened?

166
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,293
Who cares? And?

167
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:01,755
And I was wondering if, you
know, maybe one of you guys...

168
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:04,299
I'll do it.
Me, me!

169
00:07:04,341 --> 00:07:07,510
You both want to do it?
There's only room for one.

170
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:11,014
Pick me. I look great in a tux
and I will not steal focus.

171
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:12,891
No. Mike, no, no.
You want to pick me.

172
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,101
I mean... watch.

173
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:20,565
Eh?!

174
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:22,359
You know, I really don't feel
very comfortable

175
00:07:22,401 --> 00:07:23,651
making this decision.

176
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:25,153
You know,
Phoebe knows you better.

177
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:26,280
I'm going to let her choose.

178
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,784
Well, if Phoebe is choosing,
then say hello

179
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:33,912
to Mike's next groomsman.

180
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:36,957
Oh, I will.
But I will need a mirror...

181
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:38,917
as he is me.

182
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,920
Please.
You're going down.

183
00:07:41,962 --> 00:07:43,546
You are going downer.

184
00:07:43,588 --> 00:07:45,715
Is that what they say
on the figure skating team?

185
00:07:45,757 --> 00:07:47,508
I wouldn't know,
I didn't make it.

186
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:54,099
So, you know I'm filling
in for Phoebe's stepdad

187
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:55,392
tomorrow, right?

188
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:56,893
Yeah, yeah. Thanks
for doing that.

189
00:07:56,935 --> 00:07:58,561
Oh, hey, my pleasure.

190
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,064
So what are your intentions
with my Phoebe?

191
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:03,483
I intend to marry her.

192
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:05,652
Oh... a wiseacre.

193
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,446
So, I understand

194
00:08:07,486 --> 00:08:10,991
you plan to support your wife
by playing the piano?

195
00:08:12,409 --> 00:08:14,453
Isn't that kind of unstable?

196
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:16,330
No more so than acting.

197
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:17,538
Strike two.

198
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,167
You're right.

199
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,002
She probably will support me.

200
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:24,379
Hey, unless we move
in with you, Dad.

201
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,091
Strike three.

202
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,135
You only get one more, Mike.

203
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:36,057
So, what, uh,
what did you decide?

204
00:08:36,099 --> 00:08:38,768
I decided to pee.

205
00:08:38,810 --> 00:08:40,312
Mike didn't tell you?

206
00:08:40,354 --> 00:08:41,313
You have to choose
one of us to be

207
00:08:41,355 --> 00:08:42,563
in your wedding.

208
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:44,065
One of his groomsmen
fell out.

209
00:08:44,107 --> 00:08:47,652
Oh, no, no. I can't choose
between you two.

210
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:48,695
I love you both so much.

211
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:49,904
Just not enough
to put us

212
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:51,448
in the original
wedding party.

213
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:52,824
Oh...

214
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,868
But I don't want to choose.

215
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,495
It's...
Oh, okay, wait. Rach!

216
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,662
Yeah?

217
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,456
Um, Listen, I have
a very special

218
00:08:59,498 --> 00:09:01,124
bridesmaid task
for you to do.

219
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:03,877
Oh! Goodie! What is it?

220
00:09:03,918 --> 00:09:06,087
Well, there's a spot open
for only one groomsman

221
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:08,173
and you have to choose
between Ross and Chandler.

222
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,509
So, good luck with that.

223
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,552
What? What? No, no.
I don't-- don't want to do that.

224
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:14,637
All right. I guess I have
to find a new bridesmaid.

225
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:16,555
I'll do it!

226
00:09:16,597 --> 00:09:20,435
Okay, it's 2100 hours.
Time for your toasts.

227
00:09:20,477 --> 00:09:21,853
Do I have a minute
to go to the bathroom?

228
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:24,147
You had a bathroom break
at 2030.

229
00:09:24,189 --> 00:09:26,400
Pee on your own time, Mike!

230
00:09:26,441 --> 00:09:30,445
Now... in regards
to the toast, okay,

231
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:31,863
you want to keep them short.

232
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,156
Nothing kills a rehearsal dinner

233
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:34,657
like long speeches.

234
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:37,077
Okay, you just get in,
do your thing and get out.

235
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,037
Is that what you
say to Chandler?

236
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:43,458
It's 2101
and I am not amused.

237
00:09:45,877 --> 00:09:48,880
Okay, the bride and groom
have a few words

238
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:50,382
they'd like to say.

239
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,593
Okay. Hello, everyone.

240
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:57,680
And thank you all
for being here tonight.

241
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:58,890
So tomorrow's the big event.

242
00:09:58,932 --> 00:10:00,725
And some of you might not know,

243
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:02,977
but Mike and I didn't get off
to the best start.

244
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:07,815
Um, yeah, my, um...
my friend Joey and I,

245
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,734
decided to fix each other up
with friends, so...

246
00:10:09,776 --> 00:10:11,319
I-I...

247
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,615
Oh, okay. I, um...

248
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:18,617
I-I gave it a lot
of thought and I fixed him up

249
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:20,120
with my friend Mary Ellen,

250
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:21,621
who couldn't be here tonight
because...

251
00:10:21,662 --> 00:10:23,498
It's not...

252
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,334
not important.
Well, she's in rehab.

253
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:28,462
Anyway, so okay, yeah.

254
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:31,631
So, Joey said that he was fixing
me up with his friend Mike,

255
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:33,467
only he didn't
have a friend Mike,

256
00:10:33,508 --> 00:10:35,427
so he just brought,
uh, my Mike.

257
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:36,803
And, and...
( clears throat )

258
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:41,349
But despite, you know,
it got, it got good.

259
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:45,395
Okay, I want to take a moment
to mention my mother

260
00:10:45,437 --> 00:10:46,813
who couldn't be here.

261
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:48,731
Oh, God.

262
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:51,109
And... and moment's over.

263
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,819
So, okay. Um...

264
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,321
Oh, no. Forget that.

265
00:10:54,362 --> 00:10:56,531
I can forget that,
and, oh, this is funny...

266
00:10:56,573 --> 00:10:58,241
But you need to know that to...

267
00:10:58,283 --> 00:11:00,243
to get that, so...

268
00:11:00,285 --> 00:11:03,121
Oh, well, okay, um...

269
00:11:03,163 --> 00:11:05,415
I... okay...

270
00:11:05,457 --> 00:11:08,668
There... Okay, Monica,
I can't do it like this!

271
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:12,088
This is my wedding, okay?

272
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:13,756
I don't want,
I don't want this.

273
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,176
Or this. Or this.

274
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:17,636
Okay?

275
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:19,804
I just wanted a simple wedding
where my fiancé

276
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:22,056
can go to the bathroom
anytime he wants!

277
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:27,646
You know what, you're done.

278
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,272
What?
You're fired!

279
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:32,775
Cheers.

280
00:11:42,661 --> 00:11:43,744
Hey.

281
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,205
Happy wedding day!

282
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:47,040
Oh, happy my wedding day to you.

283
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:48,707
Okay, now, Joey, listen.

284
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:50,585
This is going to be
bridesmaid central,
all right?

285
00:11:50,627 --> 00:11:51,961
We're going to have
hair and makeup going on

286
00:11:52,003 --> 00:11:53,712
in the bathroom and,
uh, oh, I had to move

287
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:56,715
a couple things in the fridge
to make room for the corsages.

288
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:58,677
Oh, man.
I wouldn't have had breakfast

289
00:11:58,717 --> 00:12:00,679
if I knew there was
going to be corsages.

290
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:05,892
Hi.

291
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:08,478
Um... about last night.

292
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:12,399
I know you're
under a lot of stress,

293
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,900
and, uh, well, even though

294
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:16,695
the things you said
hurt me a little bit...

295
00:12:18,321 --> 00:12:20,240
Uh, my point is, uh,

296
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:22,701
well, I'm willing
to take my job back.

297
00:12:24,202 --> 00:12:26,162
Oh, well, that's okay.

298
00:12:27,581 --> 00:12:29,165
I think, I think you and I
will do much better

299
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:32,293
if you're just, you know,
here as a bridesmaid.

300
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:33,545
Oh.

301
00:12:33,587 --> 00:12:35,213
Is that so?

302
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:37,006
Okay.

303
00:12:37,048 --> 00:12:39,259
If that's really what
you want, then, here.

304
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,968
I give you the headset.

305
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,679
Well, I don't really want
to give you the headset.

306
00:12:42,721 --> 00:12:44,472
Yeah, well, I guess

307
00:12:44,514 --> 00:12:46,015
if you're taking over,

308
00:12:46,057 --> 00:12:48,435
then you should probably
return these messages.

309
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:49,436
Oh, this is a lot.

310
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:50,811
Uh-huh.

311
00:12:50,853 --> 00:12:52,564
But I-I'm sure you
can handle this.

312
00:12:52,606 --> 00:12:55,692
I mean, I have won awards for
my organizational skills,

313
00:12:55,734 --> 00:12:57,235
but I'm sure you'll do fine.

314
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,361
You've won awards?

315
00:12:58,403 --> 00:12:59,571
Mm-hmm.

316
00:12:59,613 --> 00:13:00,905
I printed them out
on my computer.

317
00:13:02,949 --> 00:13:04,033
Hey.
Hi.

318
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:05,034
Where's Rach?

319
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:06,369
She's in her room. Why?

320
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:07,704
Oh, I have to talk to her

321
00:13:07,746 --> 00:13:09,247
about this groomsman
situation, okay?

322
00:13:09,289 --> 00:13:10,873
I'm not gonna watch
Chandler up there

323
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:13,042
while I'm sitting in the
seats like some chump.

324
00:13:15,836 --> 00:13:16,837
( knocking )

325
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:17,922
( gasps )

326
00:13:17,964 --> 00:13:21,217
My God, you're breathtaking.

327
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,804
What do you want?

328
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:28,015
You haven't,
by any chance, chosen

329
00:13:28,057 --> 00:13:29,684
a groomsman yet, have you?

330
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:31,060
Oh, Ross,
come on, please.

331
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:33,480
Don't make this harder
than it already is.

332
00:13:33,521 --> 00:13:36,691
I'm not. I'm making
it easier. Pick me.

333
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,443
Well, Chandler said that it's
really important to him, too.

334
00:13:38,485 --> 00:13:40,194
Listen, listen.

335
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,864
Whoever you pick is going to
walk down the aisle with you.

336
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:47,494
Now, I promise, I won't say a
word, but if you pick Chandler,

337
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,828
he's going to be whispering
stupid jokes

338
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:52,332
in your ear the whole time.

339
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:54,459
Oh, you are
the lesser of two evils.

340
00:13:54,501 --> 00:13:55,543
Yes!

341
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:03,677
Sven, I don't understand
what you're saying.

342
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,261
What is wrong with the flowers?

343
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:07,846
Lorkins?
What the hell are lorkins?

344
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:09,390
♪ I know. ♪

345
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:11,892
Hey.
Listen, Mike,

346
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:13,311
if you were Swedish

347
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:14,604
and you were saying
the word "lorkins,"

348
00:14:14,646 --> 00:14:16,939
what flower would that be?

349
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:17,898
Orchids?

350
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,108
Right there.

351
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:20,568
That's why I'm marrying you.

352
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:21,902
I...

353
00:14:28,535 --> 00:14:29,577
Hello, Michael.

354
00:14:31,329 --> 00:14:32,789
Joseph.

355
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:36,459
May I have a word
with you, please?

356
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:51,098
This is... is great.

357
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,266
Have a seat.

358
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:58,606
Last night...

359
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:01,901
( Italian accent ):
I tried to welcome you
into my family.

360
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:07,114
Instead, you disrespect me.

361
00:15:08,199 --> 00:15:09,534
I cannot allow this.

362
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:11,661
Are you rehearsing

363
00:15:11,703 --> 00:15:13,954
for some really bad Mafia movie?

364
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:17,291
More back talk.

365
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:20,169
And yes, I may be
borrowing a few lines

366
00:15:20,211 --> 00:15:22,756
from my recent
unsuccessful audition

367
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:26,300
for Family Honor 2:
This-a Time, It's-a Personal.

368
00:15:29,095 --> 00:15:30,304
Joey, I kind of have
a lot to do today.

369
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:31,598
What do you,
what do you want?

370
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:33,641
I want you to
take this seriously.

371
00:15:33,683 --> 00:15:37,019
Phoebe is very, very
important to me, okay?

372
00:15:37,061 --> 00:15:38,396
And I want to make
sure that you

373
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:39,689
are going to
take care of her.

374
00:15:39,731 --> 00:15:42,191
Well... Joe,

375
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:43,735
I love Phoebe.

376
00:15:43,777 --> 00:15:46,487
She's the single most important
thing in my life.

377
00:15:46,529 --> 00:15:49,198
I'd die before I'd let
anything happen to her.

378
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:54,871
That's what I
wanted to hear,

379
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:56,623
because she's family, okay?

380
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:58,541
And now you're gonna be family,

381
00:15:58,583 --> 00:16:01,961
and there's nothing more
important in the whole world

382
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:04,297
than family.

383
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:06,674
That must have been
one lousy movie.

384
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:07,842
That was me!

385
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,221
Hi.

386
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:13,347
Hey. Can I
talk to you

387
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:14,348
about this
groomsman thing?

388
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,850
If you pick Ross, you know,

389
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,477
he'll walk you
down the aisle just fine,

390
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:21,188
but if you choose me,
you'll be getting some comedy.

391
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:26,444
Even so...

392
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:32,032
I think I'm going to pick Ross.

393
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:34,034
Let me tell you why
you need to pick me.

394
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,453
Okay.

395
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,955
( sighs )

396
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:38,957
See, when I was a kid,
you know, I was always

397
00:16:38,997 --> 00:16:41,292
left out of everything,
you know,

398
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:44,337
and it really made me feel...
insecure, you know.

399
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:48,549
I was always picked last in gym,

400
00:16:48,591 --> 00:16:50,718
even behind that big,
fat exchange student

401
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,012
who didn't even know
the rules to baseball.

402
00:16:53,053 --> 00:16:56,766
I mean, this guy would strike
out and then run to third.

403
00:16:58,935 --> 00:17:02,772
Anyway, if I'm the only one left
out of this wedding, I just know

404
00:17:02,814 --> 00:17:06,066
that all those feelings are
going to come rushing back.

405
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:10,738
All right, fine, I pick you.

406
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:13,282
Y-Y-Yes!

407
00:17:13,324 --> 00:17:17,578
Make groom for Chandler.

408
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:21,666
Oh, my.

409
00:17:23,334 --> 00:17:25,503
No, we're gonna
do it my way.

410
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:27,505
Because your way is stupid.

411
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:28,965
All right, I gotta go.

412
00:17:29,007 --> 00:17:31,050
I have another call, Reverend.

413
00:17:32,886 --> 00:17:34,554
Hello.

414
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:36,014
I'm glad we had
this little talk.

415
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,515
Yes. Yeah,

416
00:17:37,557 --> 00:17:39,809
and thanks for all the
wedding night advice.

417
00:17:39,851 --> 00:17:42,144
That didn't make me
uncomfortable at all.

418
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:44,981
All right, and so,
I-I'll see everybody tonight.

419
00:17:45,023 --> 00:17:46,399
Okay. Bye.

420
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:52,488
Uh, did you guys
know that there's

421
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:54,532
a giant ice sculpture
in the hall?

422
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:57,702
Oh, my God,
what's it doing here?

423
00:17:57,744 --> 00:17:59,579
I guess it got sent
to the billing address

424
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:00,705
as opposed
to the shipping address.

425
00:18:00,747 --> 00:18:02,832
Oh! What a pickle.

426
00:18:02,874 --> 00:18:05,376
My God. Everything's
such a mess.

427
00:18:05,418 --> 00:18:07,461
Why is this
happening to me?!

428
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:12,050
How bad do you want to stick
your tongue on that?

429
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:19,515
How's it going?

430
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:20,600
Good.

431
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,269
I'm just getting some coffee

432
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,022
so I'm alert for the wedding.

433
00:18:26,064 --> 00:18:28,024
That's what I
was doing, too.

434
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,777
Well, uh...

435
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,110
you have fun tonight.

436
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:33,111
You, too.

437
00:18:33,153 --> 00:18:35,114
Oh, I will.

438
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:36,783
Me, too.

439
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:41,662
Wait a minute.

440
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:43,247
I know why I'm
being such an ass.

441
00:18:43,289 --> 00:18:44,749
Why are you?

442
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:47,209
I'm not supposed to tell you.

443
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,003
I'm not supposed to tell you.

444
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:52,339
You told us both
we could be in the wedding?

445
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:53,507
Well...

446
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,134
In my defense...

447
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,053
you weren't supposed
to tell each other.

448
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,056
Rachel, only one
of us can do it.

449
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:01,139
You have to choose.

450
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:03,684
You and me together again.

451
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,395
Rach, Rach, knock-knock.

452
00:19:06,437 --> 00:19:07,605
Who's there?

453
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:09,107
I'll tell you
at the wedding.

454
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,985
Hey, I forgot my scarf.

455
00:19:12,026 --> 00:19:13,903
You know what?
I can't do this.

456
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:15,488
I don't know which one
of you guys to pick.

457
00:19:15,529 --> 00:19:16,823
Oh, you haven't
picked yet?

458
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,240
Oh, good, 'cause
I had, I had an idea.

459
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,659
I thought
it would be fun

460
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:23,579
if the third groomsman
was my family dog, Chappy.

461
00:19:23,621 --> 00:19:25,039
What? A dog? No.

462
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,083
Rachel gets to choose.

463
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:31,004
Wow, this is
a tough one.

464
00:19:31,045 --> 00:19:34,214
I think I'm gonna have
to go with the dog.

465
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,758
All right, wait, wait. So,
what, what you're saying

466
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,677
is that-that the chef
is at the Hamilton Club,

467
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:39,345
but the food is not,

468
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:42,682
and the drinks are there,
but the bartender is not?

469
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:46,435
Are-are-are you
freaking kidding me?!

470
00:19:46,477 --> 00:19:48,312
How's it going?

471
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:50,397
Help me.
What?

472
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,192
I want you
to be crazy bitch again.

473
00:19:54,819 --> 00:19:56,236
Really?

474
00:19:57,404 --> 00:19:58,739
Please.

475
00:19:59,866 --> 00:20:01,325
You really
want me to come back?

476
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:03,369
More than I want
to get married.

477
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:08,248
Okay, people,
we are back in business!

478
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:12,461
We have missed you so much.

479
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:14,797
Okay. Go get your hair
and makeup done

480
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:16,632
and I'll take care
of everything.

481
00:20:16,674 --> 00:20:17,967
Hey, what are
you guys gonna do?

482
00:20:18,009 --> 00:20:18,968
About what?

483
00:20:19,010 --> 00:20:19,969
The blizzard.

484
00:20:20,011 --> 00:20:21,428
I just saw on the news.

485
00:20:21,470 --> 00:20:23,181
It's like the worst
snowstorm in 20 years.

486
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:25,307
They already closed
all the bridges
and tunnels.

487
00:20:25,349 --> 00:20:26,517
What? But...

488
00:20:26,559 --> 00:20:27,727
( gasps ) But the band

489
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:28,895
and the photographer
are coming

490
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,479
all the way in from New Jersey.

491
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:32,773
I don't think they are.

492
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:34,483
Ha-ha. Looks like
you're not going

493
00:20:34,525 --> 00:20:35,943
to be in the wedding either.

494
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:39,780
So sorry, Pheebs.

495
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,586
Well, the club
lost its power.

496
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:55,295
Yeah, according to the news,
most of the city did.

497
00:20:55,337 --> 00:20:57,590
Since when
do you watch the news?

498
00:20:57,631 --> 00:20:59,217
Uh, for your information,

499
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,969
since they hired
a very hot weather girl.

500
00:21:03,137 --> 00:21:04,638
I can't believe you guys

501
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,973
aren't going to be able
to get married today.

502
00:21:06,015 --> 00:21:07,808
I know.

503
00:21:07,850 --> 00:21:09,894
RACHEL:
Well, you know, it's
so beautiful out there.

504
00:21:09,936 --> 00:21:11,896
You always wanted
to get married outside.

505
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:13,981
Why don't you guys
just do it on the street?

506
00:21:14,023 --> 00:21:15,524
What?

507
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:17,401
Well, look,
it's hardly snowing anymore.

508
00:21:17,443 --> 00:21:20,487
I mean, you couldn't ask
for a more romantic setting.

509
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:23,699
This could be the simple wedding
you've always wanted.

510
00:21:24,951 --> 00:21:26,160
What do you think?

511
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:30,414
I think I want to get
married to you today.

512
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:33,626
Me, too.

513
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,503
Monica, do you think
we could do it?

514
00:21:37,964 --> 00:21:39,590
Affirmative.

515
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:49,600
Okay, let's get
these chairs out here.

516
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:50,726
Gunther,

517
00:21:50,768 --> 00:21:52,394
hit the Christmas
lights.

518
00:21:57,150 --> 00:21:59,110
Ah...

519
00:21:59,152 --> 00:22:02,571
Okay, who left the ice sculpture

